"""One table: the current performance model scored on every validation so far (2026-11-17). No new run, no refit: every number is taken from the cited results file or recomputed from the ratios in it.
Current model = F123 form (speedups of ray orders), the one SM fit plus F123 sharing (absolute traversal, throughput), and for custom primitive programs max(throughput form, slowest warp chain) (F219) with the measured callback cost per program and input (F216 (b)).
Where a row has two forms they are two columns; no combined form was invented for this table (a combined form would need its own committed prediction).
Usage: python3 -I model/model_table.py > model/results_model_table.md"""
import math, statistics as st
def lg(r): return abs(math.log(r))          # ratio = measured / predicted
def med(x): return st.median(x)
# ratios measured/predicted, from model/priorworks/results_priorworks_diag.md and results_critical_path.md (rows in their order)
rtnn_f207 = [2.53, 2.23, 2.49, 1.69]; rtnn_b = [1.89, 1.97, 2.03, 2.42]; rtnn_launch = [0.60, 1.11, 0.87, 1.43]   # last: F220 launch event time against the same F207 prediction
tk_f207 = [3.12, 161.90, 90.72, 0.56]; tk_f219 = [0.67, 155.39, 0.46, 0.55]; tk_b = [4.83, 0.59, 127.81, 1.36]     # road5, road659, porto5, uni5
ark_f207 = [4.04, 1.73, 7.69, 3.22, 3.79, 1.31]; ark_b = [2.81, 3.48, 2.77, 3.33, 3.41, 4.70]                          # gowalla fixed/orig, glove3d fixed/orig, manuscript fixed/orig
ark_b_fixed = [2.81, 2.77, 3.41]
# speedup sets: (name, n, model rms log, baseline rms log (predict 1.0 or spread of the measured log speedups), blind?, source)
